{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "What an ask does when the hub refuses it or cannot answer it. The hub sends hive.policy.denied the instant it refuses, with source and destination context only -- no request id -- and nests the policy's own numbers under data.data. Every SDK must end the ask at once as a typed refusal rather than wait out its deadline, carry the numbers a spent quota sends, and tell an unanswered question apart from a refusal. A fire-and-forget utterance (send_utterance, send_action, send_code, or emit of recognizer_loop:utterance) has no reply and no id to track, so it counts as in flight for untracked_grace_seconds from the moment it is published -- recorded after the connection is up, since a connect that never published nothing to refuse, and kept when the publish itself errors, because a transport can fail after the hub already has the frame: its refusal could arrive while an ask is waiting. A count is a whole, non-negative number that every JSON decoder carries exactly: at most 9007199254740991 (2**53-1). Anything else -- fractional, negative, or larger -- is not a number the policy can have meant, and reads as 0. The ceiling is that low on purpose: above it a decoder backed by a double can no longer tell one whole number from the next, so two SDKs reading the same denial would report different allowances, and a contract that cannot be agreed on is not one. Wire shapes are hivemind-core _send_policy_denied / _send_backend_unavailable and hivemind-intent-quota-plugin _denied_verdict.",
  "untracked_grace_seconds": 10,
  "classification": [
    {
      "name": "an allow-list refusal names the type and carries no quota",
      "event": {
        "type": "hive.policy.denied",
        "data": {
          "denied_type": "recognizer_loop:utterance",
          "code": "acl_disallowed_type",
          "reason": "recognizer_loop:utterance not in allowed_types",
          "data": {
            "allowed": [
              "speak",
              "ovos.skills.fallback.list"
            ]
          }
        },
        "context": {
          "source": "hivemind-core",
          "destination": "sat-1"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "refused",
        "denied_type": "recognizer_loop:utterance",
        "code": "acl_disallowed_type",
        "reason": "recognizer_loop:utterance not in allowed_types",
        "allowed": [
          "speak",
          "ovos.skills.fallback.list"
        ],
        "quota": null
      }
    },
